The user will ask something like: "I'm using you to help me file my 2023 taxes. Here's my situation: I'm single, live in Minneapolis MN, and my W-2 from Summit Financial shows $75,600 in wages. I also had $9,800 in 1099-NEC freelance w..."

Use topic-level wording in the rule you want stored (e.g. "taxes, filing, deductions, IRS" not just "taxes") so it generalizes to other phrasings.


